{"title":"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A particle moves through the first quadrant as follows. During the first minute it moves from the origin to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Thereafter, it continues to follow the directions indicated in the figure, going back and forth between the positive x and y axes, moving one unit of distance parallel to an axis in each minute. At which point will the particle be after exactly 1989 minutes?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b59fc45d3e82134723e6aeede797eafa9e65567d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; Label f; f.p=fontsize(6);  xaxis(0,3.5,Ticks(f, 1.0));  yaxis(0,4.5,Ticks(f, 1.0));  draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--(0,2)--(2,2)--(2,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--(0,4)--(1.5,4),blue+linewidth(2)); arrow((2,4),dir(180),blue); [/asy]\" width=\"522\" height=\"668\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37bdc9c15dc235df7e7f0de72398e2e6afea0ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ (35,44)\\qquad\\text{(B)}\\ (36,45)\\qquad\\text{(C)}\\ (37,45)\\qquad\\text{(D)}\\ (44,35)\\qquad\\text{(E)}\\ (45,36)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"580\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Squares of size <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/c/9bcac678f2cafc58a99877017ad20bd261c2db06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\times1,\\ 2\\times2,\\ 3\\times3,\\ ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"17\" /> are successively enclosed between the path and the axes.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00c48f86de6b301f3b223ff2c0285b404447a0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; axialshade((0,0)--(0,3)--(3,3)--(3,0)--cycle,yellow,(-6,-6),white,(3,3)); axialshade((0,0)--(0,2)--(2,2)--(2,0)--cycle,orange,(-3,-3),white,(2,2)); axialshade((0,0)--(0,1)--(1,1)--(1,0)--cycle,red,(-2,-2),white,(1,1)); Label f; f.p=fontsize(6);  xaxis(0,3.5,Ticks(f, 1.0));  yaxis(0,4.5,Ticks(f, 1.0)); draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1),red+linewidth(2)); draw((0,1)--(0,2)--(2,2)--(2,0),orange+linewidth(2)); draw((2,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3),yellow+linewidth(2)); draw((0,3)--(0,4)--(1.5,4),green+linewidth(2)); arrow((2,4),dir(180),green); dot((0,1),red);dot((2,0),orange);dot((0,3),yellow); [/asy]\" width=\"522\" height=\"668\" />\n</p><p>It takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8bdd636bb65f59a127de5a5c71541582b56513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+1+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> minutes to enclose the first square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/270d656813b60d5c84c1c68a5c67be595f432bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> minutes to enclose the second, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5face202e76ba72aa373b7c49a080666634c33a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+3+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> minutes to enclose the third, and so on. After odd squares, the particle is on the Y axis; after even squares, the particle is on the X axis.\n</p><p>First we find the highest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6d7eae7718439c21b473cafbbe02c7184bac295.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^n1+2k\\le1989$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"142\" height=\"53\" />. The sum is equal to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a094c00816602bdcbb729e5eef40c9db981ba6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^n1+2\\sum_{k=1}^nk=n+n(n+1)=n(n+2)=(n+1)^2-1\\]\" width=\"445\" height=\"48\" />\nso the highest value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1d89cbbc3793da01563d4fbb706ad8262cd43cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> for which the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/6184f03128b60c6d13c71ad8bd2871baecbd3f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1935$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/6184f03128b60c6d13c71ad8bd2871baecbd3f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1935$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> minutes the 43rd square is enclosed and the particle is at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a3718d99e36b8204a340b986fe357ca4a7fd960c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,43)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />. During the 1936th minute it moves up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/b/a6b69f1def5e0c04d48ada535aa3fbb2a79c77a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,44)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />. At the end of the 1980th minute it has moved right to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ee5c5f92420d9fc7a3727c3a7eb6f0bdc8d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(44,44)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />. After this it moves downward, and at the end of the 1989th minute it is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0afffd65291da1f7eb17e59c8bd403aa452950cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(44,35)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that it takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcd2ce13b1c7e9381e3b59ae45582136ca2eae9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> minutes to travel to any point in the format <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/6026bfa7d4fdad9bd3583800933de52f3443641d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> &lt;-- aka the top-right corners of the \"square-like\" shapes. (try this yourself if you dont believe it)\n</p><p>Additionally, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by 2, the next step would be to go down parallel to the y-axis from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/6026bfa7d4fdad9bd3583800933de52f3443641d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" />. Else, the next step would be to go left parallel to the x-axis from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/6026bfa7d4fdad9bd3583800933de52f3443641d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" />. We now find a value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f34f1a169206471652de3084d316bad14dc6bf77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+n = n(n+1) \\le 1989$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e61070e07eb3e7672e6bd5ab08967c0571749b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40^2 = 1600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. After testing values over 40, we notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/980f63a4840e570d3888dc340606b32043743774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44(44+1) = 1980$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore it takes 1980 seconds to move to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ee5c5f92420d9fc7a3727c3a7eb6f0bdc8d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(44,44)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by 2, we just need to move down <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0c5e7252de80a9514649c2c8fb08f0ccf4be5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(44, 44)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, yielding the final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME\" title=\"1989 AHSME\">1989 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017025139\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 236/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6840/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.955      1 -total\n 55.08%    7.135      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 43.28%    5.607      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11382:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017025139 and revision id 264471. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}